===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:it<ety:inh<ang:hit>>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|it}}, {{m|enm|hit}} ( > dialectal {{cog|en|hit|t=it}}), from {{inh|en|ang|hit|t=it}}, from  {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*hit}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*hit|t=this, this one}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*ḱe|t=here; here}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|yol|it}}, {{m|yol|t'}}, {{m|yol|yt|t=it}}, {{cog|frr|at}}, {{m|frr|et}}, {{m|frr|'t|t=it}}, {{cog|stq|et|t=it}}, {{cog|fy|it|t=it}}, {{cog|nl|het|t=it}}, {{cog|lb|hatt|t=her, it, she}}, {{cog|ovd|eð|t=it}}; also {{cog|pgl|ᚕᚑᚔ|t=here}}, {{cog|la|cis|t=short of; before}}, {{m|la|hic|t=this}}, {{cog|el|εκείνος|t=that; those}}. Compare {{cog|cim|es}}, {{m|cim|is}}, {{m|cim|'s}}, {{m|cim|'z|t=it}}, {{cog|de|es}}, {{m|de|'s|t=it, there}}, {{cog|mhn,wym|s|t=it}}, {{cog|yi|עס|t=it}}, {{cog|fo|ið|t=that, which, who}}, {{cog|got|𐌹𐍄𐌰|t=it}}, which instead descends from {{ncog|gem-pro|*it|t=it}}. More at {{l|en|he}}.
